                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 229.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of an article contained in No</hi>. 191
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of “El Nacional” of July</hi> 15, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">of this city, forwarded herewith.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center">THE FOURTH OF JULY.</p>
                <p>This glorious day, the anniversary of the declaration of the independence of the
                    United States of America, the model of the modern republics, was observed by the
                    Hon. Mr. Wing in a most becoming manner.</p>
                <p>On the previous evening his house was serenaded by the bands of the two bodies of
                    soldiery now stationed in this city, who were generously treated by him. On the
                    day of the 4th he received congratulatory visits from all the most eminent
                    members of Quitonian society. But aside from the just motives that all true
                    republicans had for felicitation upon that notable day, was the fact that the
                    Hon. Mr. Wing has established such pleasant relations, and is so universally
                    respected, and enjoys such genuine popularity here.</p>
            </div>
